8. WHATSAPP ORDERING — CRITICAL REQUIREMENT

For the first version, Zestro will accept orders through WhatsApp.

Official WhatsApp order number:

+880 1601-987672

Use this WhatsApp link format:

https://wa.me/8801601987672

When the customer presses "Place Order" or "Send Order on WhatsApp":

1. Validate checkout information.
2. Calculate the final order total.
3. Generate a unique order reference.
4. Save an order record in Firestore with status "awaiting_whatsapp_confirmation".
5. Build a properly formatted WhatsApp message.
6. Open WhatsApp with the prepared message.
7. Ask the customer to press Send inside WhatsApp.

Do not claim that the order is confirmed merely because WhatsApp opened.

Show this message to the customer:

"Your order message is ready! Please press SEND in WhatsApp to contact Zestro. Your order will be confirmed once our team accepts it."

WhatsApp message format

Generate a clear message similar to:

Hello Zestro! I would like to place an order.

ORDER REFERENCE: ZES-XXXXXXXX

ORDER TYPE: DINE IN / TAKEAWAY / DELIVERY

CUSTOMER DETAILS:
Name:
Phone:
Address: (Delivery only)
Table Number: (When available)

ORDER DETAILS:

1. Product Name
   Variant / Size:
   Customisations:
   Special Instructions:
   Quantity:
   Unit Price:
   Total:

2. Product Name
   Variant / Size:
   Customisations:
   Quantity:
   Unit Price:
   Total:

Subtotal:
Delivery Charge:
Other Charges:
Discount:
TOTAL: ৳XXXX

Thank you!

Use properly encoded URL parameters and handle special characters safely.

Prefer a reliable new-tab WhatsApp handoff. Handle browser popup restrictions gracefully.

If saving the order to Firestore fails, do not pretend it was saved. Explain the problem and provide a safe WhatsApp fallback where possible.

Important operational rule

WhatsApp links cannot tell the website whether the customer actually pressed Send or whether Zestro accepted the order.

Therefore:

- Initially save orders as "awaiting_whatsapp_confirmation".
- Admin staff manually verify the incoming WhatsApp message.
- Staff can mark the order Confirmed, Preparing, Ready, Completed or Cancelled.
- Never automatically mark an order as confirmed after opening WhatsApp.

Do not implement a fake WhatsApp API integration. Direct WhatsApp Cloud API automation can be added later.

